 ## Overview
-This method constructs a perspective projection matrix that maps view space coordinates to clip space while utilizing a reversed depth buffer (Reverse Z) and an effectively infinite far plane [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of depth precision loss at large distances inherent in standard finite-far-plane projections, thereby avoiding far-plane clipping artifacts and maintaining high precision near the camera [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard perspective projections by inverting the depth range and removing the far-plane dependency from the matrix structure [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Custom Perspective Projection Matrix Construction](2175-custom-perspective-projection-matrix-construction.md).
